"output_tokens":671,"requests":1}},{"kind":"resumed","lineage":{"dependencies":[],"digest":"24fe44c81975d7ba0b0068df84bb0b3c5551ae0fe289d6723ef4d9d38cca2351"},"namespace_version":1,"reason":null,"unit_id":"agent:T3","usage":{"input_tokens":25115,"output_tokens":981,"requests":2}}],"version":1},"findings":[{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"State the concrete enforcement mechanism for AC5's reserved tail budget in a sequential shell probe (e.g. an absolute run deadline each section checks and self-skips against, and/or publishing the reserved-tail metrics before the heavy docker walk), showing why an earlier blocked timeout-wrapped call cannot consume the reserved tail window.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.2,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["AC5: 'Committed mechanism: a reserved tail budget that no earlier section can spend — reordering alone only moves which metric starves.'","observability.sh is a straight-line sequential script: metrics are published in file order via successive `aws cloudwatch put-metric-data` calls (e.g. root_disk at :191, docker_storage at :596-602), with no scheduler/watchdog that could interrupt a blocked earlier section to hand control to the tail.","AC2 asks 'how it is enforced' but does not connect that enforcement to AC5's reserved-budget claim; a reader could implement AC5 as reorder-plus-comment and pass neither the intent nor AC5's own caveat."],"finding":"AC5's committed mechanism ('a reserved tail budget that no earlier section can spend') is named but its ENFORCEMENT in a non-preemptive, sequential, single-process shell script is unspecified. In straight-line bash, if an earlier timeout-wrapped section blocks for its full ceiling, the tail section never starts — no budget 'reservation' can preempt an already-running blocked call. The plan must state the concrete enforcement path (e.g. an absolute start-of-run deadline that each section reads and self-skips when it would cross the reserved tail window, publishing a 'skipped' signal; or publishing the reserved-tail metrics before the heavy walk) so the mechanism actually delivers position-independence rather than merely re-labelling reordering, which AC5 itself says is insufficient.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fa552c08c7e9f7cc4","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance criteria, AC5 ('Metric publication no longer depends on position … reserved tail budget')","norm_id":"nb7a2660a7fb8e647","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["An earlier section (e.g. the twice-called docker_du_bytes) consumes its full 2x120s timeout ceiling; with only a passive 'reserved' budget the tail section still never runs, so mem_used_percent/mirror_out_of_sync remain truncated exactly as today.","Implementer reorders sections and adds a comment reserving N seconds for the tail, believing AC5 satisfied, but under I/O load an earlier blocked call still eats the wall clock and the tail starves."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Specify that at start-of-run the probe computes an absolute deadline = start + (TimeoutStartSec - TAIL_RESERVE); every section, before beginning, compares `now` to (deadline) and if it cannot finish within remaining budget it skips and emits the AC4 truncation signal instead of blocking; the reserved TAIL_RESERVE window is then guaranteed available to the tail section regardless of upstream blocking. Alternatively move the tail metrics ahead of the heavy docker/journal walks so their publication is unconditional.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"underspecified_oracle","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"underspecified_certification","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"high"}}},{"block_threshold":null,"blocking_enabled":null,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["P6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":null,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["1 criterion line(s) bundle multiple deliverables with 'and' (split so each is independently verifiable)."],"finding":"Acceptance-criteria / definition-of-done quality issues.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f607dd457c67f9209","impact":0.4,"is_primary":null,"location":"","norm_id":"ned06ebc801a522e3","priority":0.4,"reason":null,"recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Split compound criteria, replace subjective terms with observable outcomes, and state how each is verified.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"State the concrete remediation levers that bring the summed bounds under 240s (e.g. dedupe the double docker_du_bytes walk, lower named ceilings, or parallelize) so AC2's 'provably below' is reachable by a described step, not left to executor discretion.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5a","T5b","T5e"],"criteria":["E2","E6"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.734,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'Summing every ceiling in the file gives over 495s inside a 240s timeout'","'docker_du_bytes is called TWICE ... 2 x 120 = 240s = TimeoutStartSec exactly'","AC2 states the sum must be 'provably below TimeoutStartSec' but no step describes how the sum is brought under budget"],"finding":"AC2 ('sum of wall-clock bounds provably below TimeoutStartSec') and AC5 ('reserved tail budget') require actually reducing the cumulative budget from 495s+ to under 240s, but the plan does not commit to WHICH levers achieve that reduction — e.g. deduping the two docker_du_bytes calls (observability.sh:592-593 over $DOCKER_ROOT and $DOCKER_ROOT/overlay2, alone 2x120=240s = the entire budget), lowering per-call ceilings, or parallelizing sections. The remediation design is left to the executor.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f22955858c68ad518","impact":0.264,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance criteria, AC2/AC5; body 'The mechanism is CUMULATIVE'","norm_id":"n8868769358199961","priority":0.066,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Executor measures cumulative attribution (AC1) then must invent the reduction strategy to satisfy AC2, possibly diverging from author intent"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Add a body paragraph and/or AC naming the specific budget-reduction mechanism — at minimum eliminate the redundant second docker_du_bytes pass over $DOCKER_ROOT/overlay2 (the ~1.88M-file tree is essentially the same), and enumerate the resulting bound sum against the 240s budget with the reserved tail margin.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.25,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radi